/-!
# Serre's global generation theorem for ample line bundles

On a scheme `X`, twisting any quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `F` of finite type by a sufficiently
high tensor power of an ample invertible sheaf `L` makes `F ⊗ L^⊗n` globally generated by finitely
many sections: there is an epimorphism `𝒪_X^J ⟶ F ⊗ L^⊗n` from a free sheaf of finite rank
(Hartshorne, Theorem II.5.17; Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3).

Given a finite affine cover of `X` by nonvanishing loci `X_{sᵢ}` of sections `sᵢ ∈ Γ(X, L^{⊗dᵢ})`
with `dᵢ > 0` (`LineBundleClass.IsAmple.exists_finset_isAffineOpen_nonvanishingLocus`), passing to
the common multiple `D = ∏ dᵢ` replaces each `sᵢ` by a positive power in `L^{⊗D}` with the same
nonvanishing locus (`InvertibleSheaf.exists_nonvanishingLocus_eq_of_mk_eq_pow`). Applying the
single-bundle global generation theorem
(`Scheme.Modules.eventually_exists_generatingSections_tensor_tensorPow`) to `L^{⊗D}` and each of
the `D` twists `F ⊗ L^{⊗r}` (`0 ≤ r < D`) yields a uniform bound `n₀` for all `n ≥ n₀`.

Applying the theorem to a line bundle `K` shows that `K ⊗ L^{⊗n}` and `L^{⊗n}` are globally
generated for all sufficiently large `n`. Tensoring a surjection `𝒪_X^J ⟶ F ⊗ M` by an inverse
`M'` (`M ⊗ M' ≅ 𝒪_X`) yields an epimorphism `⨁_{j ∈ J} M' ⟶ F`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_epi_free_tensorPow_of_isAmple`: Serre's global
  generation theorem for an ample line bundle.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_epi_biproduct_of_epi_free_tensor`: dualizing an
  epimorphism `𝒪_X^J ⟶ F ⊗ M` into an epimorphism `⨁_J M' ⟶ F`.
* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleSheaf.exists_isGloballyGenerated_tensorProduct_tensorPow`
  and `exists_isGloballyGenerated_tensorPow`: high ample twists of any line bundle (and high
  powers of an ample line bundle) are globally generated.

## References

* R. Hartshorne, *Algebraic Geometry*, GTM 52, Springer, 1977, Theorem II.5.17.
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3).
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory Limits MonoidalCategory BraidedCategory AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
  TopologicalSpace TauCeti

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

